
How to set up the client
------------------------

1. Go to directory <client-code>
cd <client-code>

2. Edit (a copy of) configs/generic/client.yaml
You have to set a few parameters of the client:
    <name-of-engine>   name of your Go engine (may contain spaces)
    <command-line>     command to start the engine, with all arguments
    <server-host>      name of the machine running the server
    <server-port>      port number, determines the server's board size
    <server-user>      your user name on the server (no account necessary)
    <server-password>  your password for this user
The files simple.yaml and sample.yaml contain examples.
I will refer to the modified copy as 'my_client.yaml'.

3. Start Go client
python src/cgosclient.py configs/generic/my_client.yaml &
This will also start the Go engine.

4. Stop Go client
cp killfiles/kill_client .
This will also stop the Go engine.
The kill file will be automatically deleted.

